RCF- request for comments- this defines the rules of networking
RCF 2460 ----> IPV6 specifications
Treminologies of RCF are: nodes->that impliments ipv6
                          Router -> a node that forwards IPv6 packets not explicitly addressed to itself.
                          Host -> any node that is not a router. 
                          
routers can have multiple IP and mac address based on the no. of interfaces or networks it is connected to.
router has a table called routing table that has routes in it.

Router uses three diff. ways to propogate data 
1.Direct method : where the router is directly connected to the interfaces like left and rright interfaces
2.Static method : where an administrator helps with the updating routing table in a indirectly connected interfaces
3.Dynamic method: where the routers themself share the interface details that they have .
